Under **NC Medicaid Clinical Coverage Policy 10A**, outpatient therapy services must have a **treatment plan (plan of care)** that includes all of the following:

- the **start and end date** of the therapy treatment plan, with a duration of **no more than six months**;
- the **discipline-specific treatment diagnosis** and any related medical diagnoses;
- the beneficiary’s **rehabilitative or habilitative potential**;
- **defined goals** for each therapy discipline that are **specific, measurable, and reasonably expected to be achieved** within the plan period;
- the **skilled interventions, methodology, procedures, and specific programs** to be used;
- the **frequency of services**;
- the **length of each treatment visit in minutes**; and
- the **name, credentials, and signature** of the professional completing the treatment plan, **dated on or before the plan start date**. [[Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)]

In addition, Policy 10A’s documentation section requires that the provider keep **a copy of the treatment plan** in the record. [[Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)]

**Current source:** Clinical Coverage Policy 10A, effective **February 1, 2025**; I checked for amendments and the tool returned **10A as the authoritative current document**. [[Clinical Coverage Policy 10A](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/10a-outpatient-specialized-therapies/download?attachment)]

